@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+1. **P1 — The plan misses the total `PublicArticle` key inventory.** Adding optional `matter` to `PublicArticle` will fail typechecking because `WIRE_ROW` must cover every key ([tests/shared-inventory.test.ts:353](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/tests/shared-inventory.test.ts:353), [tests/shared-inventory.test.ts:446](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/tests/shared-inventory.test.ts:446)). The plan’s test list does not mention this ([plan:58](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/docs/plans/261018l-visitors-on-a-shared-link-get-the-front-and-back-matter-folds.md:58)). **Fix:** add `matter` to `WIRE_ROW`, probably mapped to `"text"`, and amend that inventory row’s copy to disclose that stored front/back-matter classifications affect folding ([src/messages.ts:5197](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/messages.ts:5197)). Add `tests/shared-inventory.test.ts` to the plan.
+
+2. **P2 — “Nothing the model wrote” is materially inaccurate.** The model answers with ranges/sections, block IDs and kinds ([src/matter.ts:73](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/matter.ts:73)); those judgments are combined and stored as the stretches proposed for publication ([src/matter-step.ts:133](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/matter-step.ts:133), [src/matter-step.ts:139](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/matter-step.ts:139)). What does *not* cross is free-form model prose, provider output, generator, versions, hashes and failure reasons. The IDs already identify public blocks and kinds are closed, so I see no sensitive disclosure—but structured model-derived classification does cross. **Fix:** replace the claim at [plan:31](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/docs/plans/261018l-visitors-on-a-shared-link-get-the-front-and-back-matter-folds.md:31) with that narrower statement, and reflect it in the sharing inventory.
+
+3. **P2 — The provenance-withholding test is assigned to the wrong boundary, and the hash-parity positive control is underspecified.** The proposed DTO receives only `MatterStretchStored[]`; `version`, `generator`, `sourceHash`, `modelUnavailable` and `reason` have already been discarded by `matterForReader`, which reconstructs each stretch field by field ([src/matter-current.ts:83](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/matter-current.ts:83), [src/matter-current.ts:95](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/matter-current.ts:95)). A DTO-only test cannot prove the stored document’s top-level fields stay behind. **Fix:** in the public-reader/Postgres test, store a full current document containing every provenance field and assert the returned public payload contains only `{from,to,kinds}`. Compute its hash from the owner read, then load it publicly using fixture blocks with a non-null `level` and `role`; those optional fields are the easiest for a mapper to omit without a type error. Keep the DTO test for planted extra fields inside individual stretches.
+
+4. **P3 — The plan’s raw-versus-sanitised hash explanation is false, although the proposed implementation is sound.** `matterInputHash` reads only `id, text, kind, level, words, role` ([src/matter-current.ts:52](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/matter-current.ts:52)); sanitisation changes only `html` ([src/sanitize.ts:167](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/sanitize.ts:167)). Therefore raw rows and sanitised blocks produce the same matter hash. The public query does carry all six fields—`blockId` supplies `id`, followed by `kind`, `level`, `text`, `words`, and `role` ([src/store/public-reader.ts:885](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/store/public-reader.ts:885))—matching the owner query ([src/store/pg.ts:1656](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/store/pg.ts:1656)). **Fix:** correct [plan:74](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/docs/plans/261018l-visitors-on-a-shared-link-get-the-front-and-back-matter-folds.md:74): using `blocks` is preferable because they are already the payload being validated, not because sanitisation changes the hash. Extend the hash unit test to cover `id` and `role`, which its current field-change test omits ([tests/matter.test.ts:106](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/tests/matter.test.ts:106)).
+
+5. **P3 — The leaf move has more stale source references than the plan lists.** Besides `types.ts` and `matter-view.ts`, comments still locate `matterForReader` or `MATTER_PROMPT_VERSION` in `matter-step.ts`, including [src/store/pg.ts:1282](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/store/pg.ts:1282), [src/store/pg-revisions.ts:404](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/store/pg-revisions.ts:404), and [tests/freshness-deciders-agree.test.ts:142](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/tests/freshness-deciders-agree.test.ts:142). **Fix:** include an `rg` sweep for the moved symbol names and update every ownership/source reference to `matter-current.ts`.
+
+The leaf itself is sound: `node:crypto`, `matter-shape.ts`, and type-only imports do not reach a gateway, while importing either old module would. `resolveAccess` already spreads the public payload into the common `Article`, so no additional client seam is needed. The head/OG read is deliberately a separate projection without blocks or rendering data ([src/store/public-reader.ts:534](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/store/public-reader.ts:534)), so it should not receive `matter`. Export already selects every active revision column and writes non-separated columns into `content/revision.json` ([src/store/revision-columns.ts:33](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/store/revision-columns.ts:33), [src/store/export-bundle.ts:413](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/qi-8y3tx5tp-public-matter-folds/src/store/export-bundle.ts:413)); `matter` therefore already exports. I do not see a simpler design than the pure leaf without duplicating freshness policy.
+
+VERDICT: revise
